Code imported from skymp (https://github.com/skyrim-multiplayer/skymp, commit 2849e676) keeps
skymp's terms. ORIGINS.md lists every imported file with its licence.
- Code from skymp5-server is under AGPL-3.0 as published by skymp (LICENSE is skymp5-server's
  licence text).
- Engine/Shared/viet, Engine/Server/libespm and Engine/Server/papyrus-vm are under the MIT licence
  in the LICENSE file of each folder.
- Engine/Shared/serialization and Engine/Tests/unit come from skymp folders that have no licence
  file, and skymp states no licence for them: TERMS.md says the project is primarily distributed
  under the GPLv3 and AGPLv3 and points to a licence file in each subproject folder, which these two
  lack. The unit tests are skymp5-server's tests; they fell under skymp's root GPL-3.0 licence from
  2021-06-26 until the per-subproject split of 2022-03-30. serialization was written in 2024. SUG
  imports both and credits skymp as their source.
- Engine/vcpkg/ports/makeid/MakeID.h (Emil Persson, Humus) is in the public domain.

Libraries installed by vcpkg are linked statically into the binaries built from this repository.
Their licence texts are in out/build/<preset>/vcpkg_installed/x64-windows-static-v145/share/<port>/
and must ship with any binary distribution. antigo is under LGPL-3.0.
The npm packages of Engine/Server/host (package-lock.json) are bundled into
bin/server/skymp5-server.js. Their licence texts are in Engine/Server/host/node_modules/<package>/
after the build and must ship with any distribution of the bundle.

No Bethesda game files are included. Game data is read from the user's own Skyrim installation.
The .pex files in Engine/Server/standard_scripts are small stubs compiled by skymp's author (they
declare each script class and its parent), not Bethesda scripts.
